window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f06621b97709dae2"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">技能与插件</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>技能和插件可以为 ChatGPT 与 Codex 提供合适的指令、资源和工具，帮助它们完成可重复的工作。这样，你就不必在每次对话中反复粘贴相同的提示词、模板、要求或流程。</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pKwRNdDtai0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看：ChatGPT 中的插件（需联网）</a></p> <ul> <li><strong>技能（skill）</strong>：为特定任务或工作流打包的指令及其支持资源。</li> <li><strong>插件（plugin）</strong>：可安装的软件包，可以包含技能和 Model Context Protocol（MCP）服务器。MCP 服务器会提供工具，也可以选择性地包含自定义 ChatGPT 界面。插件还可以包含供 Codex 运行时（包括 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex）使用的<a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">生命周期钩子</a>。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"use-skills-for-repeatable-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">用技能处理可重复的工作</h2> <p>技能是一种可重复使用的工作流，可以为 ChatGPT 或 Codex 提供针对特定任务的指导。它能记录你经常执行的工作方式，让产品在每次遇到相应任务时都遵循同一套流程。</p> <p>一个技能可以包含：</p> <ul> <li>帮助 ChatGPT 和 Codex 识别适用场景的名称与说明。</li> <li>定义执行步骤和预期结果的工作流指令。</li> <li>模板、示例、品牌指南、架构模式或已连接工具等支持资源。</li> </ul> <p>当高质量结果依赖于可重复的方法时，技能尤其有用。例如：准备每日简报、审阅文档、制作演示文稿、遵循团队写作规范，或从相同的已连接工具获取信息。</p> <p>使用技能可以提高一致性、让团队最佳实践在工作流中随时可用，并通过统一标准取代未记录的个人流程。</p> <p>当你的请求与某个技能的用途相符时，ChatGPT 和 Codex 可以自动选择它。你也可以手动指定：ChatGPT 支持 <code>@</code> 提及，Codex 支持 <code>$</code> 形式的技能调用。</p> <p><a id=\"build-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">构建技能</h2> <p>你可以把自己已经反复执行的任务整理成一份聚焦的操作手册，从而开始创建实用技能。适合作为起点的例子包括每周更新、营销简报、会议跟进，以及任何需要固定步骤和格式的任务。</p> <ol> <li><strong>选择一个明确的任务。</strong> 记录你通常从什么材料开始，例如文件、链接或笔记，并说明完成后应该得到什么结果。</li> <li><strong>描述工作流。</strong> 在 ChatGPT 中，使用 <code>@skill-creator</code>；在 Codex 中，使用 <code>$skill-creator</code>。说明目标、执行步骤、预期格式，以及始终应包含或避免的内容。也可以添加模板或优秀示例。</li> <li><strong>审阅并试用草稿。</strong> 检查指令，使用真实任务进行测试，并在结果不符合预期时调整。</li> <li><strong>安装并重复使用。</strong> 技能启用后，ChatGPT 或 Codex 可以在适用时使用它；如果工作区设置允许，也可以与团队成员共享。</li> </ol> <p>如需了解更多信息，请参阅下方的技能构建指南。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\"><strong>构建技能</strong><br>创建、测试并分享可重复使用的技能。</a></p> <p><a id=\"use-plugins-for-tools-and-shared-workflows\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">用插件连接工具并共享工作流</h2> <p>插件让可重复使用的能力更容易安装和分享。一个插件可以将技能与 MCP 服务器组合起来，为 GitHub、Google Drive 或 Slack 等服务提供工具和上下文。</p> <p>ChatGPT 和 Codex 共用一个通用插件目录。若要添加现成工作流，可以先浏览该目录，而不必从头构建。安装插件后，你可以直接描述任务，或者根据当前界面的调用方式明确选择插件或其内含技能。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">了解如何安装和使用插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-between-a-skill-and-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">如何在技能和插件之间选择</h2> <p>如果你需要针对一个明确任务重复使用的指令，请使用技能。如果你需要一个可安装的软件包，并希望将技能与已连接的服务组合起来，请使用插件。</p> <p>如需在 ChatGPT 对话中构建插件，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p>如果你准备迁移现有的自定义 GPT 工作流，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">将自定义 GPT 迁移到插件</a>，了解工作区准备、迁移、测试和共享。</p> <p>你还可以使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">Record &amp; Replay</a> 演示工作流，并将录制内容转化为可重复使用的技能。若要打包并分发自己的软件包，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p>如果插件需要连接服务或提供 MCP 工具，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建 MCP 服务器</a>。插件准备好接受公开审核后，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/submission.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">提交插件</a>。</p> <p>如需查看更多示例，请参阅 <a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy 中的技能用法（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Skills and plugins help ChatGPT and Codex complete repeatable work with the right instructions, resources, and tools. They reduce the need to paste the same prompt, template, requirements, or process into every chat.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pKwRNdDtai0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch: Plugins in ChatGPT (online)</a></p> <ul> <li>A <strong>skill</strong> packages instructions and supporting resources for a specific task or workflow.</li> <li>A <strong>plugin</strong> is an installable bundle that can include skills and Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. MCP servers expose tools and can optionally include custom ChatGPT UI. Plugins can also include <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">lifecycle hooks</a> for the Codex runtime, including ChatGPT Work and Codex.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"use-skills-for-repeatable-work\">Use skills for repeatable work</h2> <p>A skill is a reusable workflow that gives ChatGPT or Codex task-specific guidance. It can capture the way you already perform recurring work so either product follows the same process whenever that task comes up.</p> <p>A skill can combine:</p> <ul> <li>A name and description that help ChatGPT and Codex recognize when the skill applies.</li> <li>Workflow instructions that define the process and expected result.</li> <li>Supporting resources such as templates, examples, brand guidance, schemas, or connected tools.</li> </ul> <p>Skills are most useful when good results depend on a repeatable approach. For example, a skill can prepare a daily brief, review documentation, create a presentation, apply a team writing standard, or gather information from the same connected tools each week.</p> <p>Use skills to improve consistency, make team best practices available in the workflow, and share a standard process instead of relying on undocumented knowledge.</p> <p>ChatGPT and Codex can choose a skill when your request matches its purpose. You can also select one explicitly. ChatGPT supports <code>@</code> mentions, while Codex supports <code>$</code> mentions for skills.</p> <h2 id=\"build-skills\">Build skills</h2> <p>You can start by turning a task you already repeat into a focused playbook for ChatGPT and Codex. Good first skills include a weekly update, a campaign brief, a meeting follow-up, or any task where the steps and format should stay consistent.</p> <p>To build a useful skill:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Choose one focused task.</strong> Note what you normally start with, such as files, links, or notes, and what a finished result should look like.</li> <li><strong>Describe the workflow.</strong> In ChatGPT, start with <code>@skill-creator</code>; in Codex, use <code>$skill-creator</code>. Explain the goal, the steps to follow, the expected format, and anything the skill should always include or avoid. Add a template or a good example when you have one.</li> <li><strong>Review and try the draft.</strong> Check the instructions, test the skill with a realistic request, and refine it if the result misses a step or drifts from the format you want.</li> <li><strong>Install and reuse it.</strong> Once the skill is enabled, ChatGPT or Codex can use it for relevant requests, or you can select it explicitly. You can also share it with teammates when your workspace settings allow it.</li> </ol> <p>For more details on building skills, see our dedicated guide below.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\"><strong>Build skills</strong><br>Create, test, and share reusable skills with ChatGPT and Codex.</a></p> <h2 id=\"use-plugins-for-tools-and-shared-workflows\">Use plugins for tools and shared workflows</h2> <p>Plugins make reusable capabilities easier to install and share. A plugin can combine skills with MCP servers for tools and context from services such as GitHub, Google Drive, or Slack.</p> <p>ChatGPT and Codex share one universal plugin directory. Browse it when you want to add an existing workflow instead of building one yourself. After installing a plugin, describe the task directly or explicitly choose a plugin or bundled skill using the invocation syntax for your surface.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Learn how to install and use plugins</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-between-a-skill-and-a-plugin\">Choose between a skill and a plugin</h2> <p>Use a skill when you need reusable instructions for a focused task. Use a plugin when you want an installable package that can combine instructions with connected services or other tools.</p> <p>To build a plugin through a conversation in ChatGPT, see <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">Build plugins</a>.</p> <p>Moving an existing custom GPT workflow? See <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">Migrate custom GPTs to plugins</a> for workspace preparation, migration, testing, and sharing.</p> <p>You can also demonstrate a workflow with <a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">Record &amp; Replay</a>, which turns the recording into a reusable skill. To package and distribute your own bundle, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a>.</p> <p>If your plugin needs to connect to a service or expose MCP tools, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build an MCP server</a>. When your plugin is ready for public review, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/submission.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Submit plugins</a>.</p> <p>For more examples of reusable workflows, see <a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Using skills in OpenAI Academy (online)</a>.</p>"};
